title: Placeholder colors for tiles
intro: A tilemap with no image can now give each tile number a color of its own, so a level's floors and walls can be blocked out before there's any art.
project: Empty | Blockout

chapter: A color for each tile | Placeholder Colors
create: Tilemap
set: Transform.Position = 0, 0, 0
set: Tilemap.Tint = #FFFFFF
look: 5, -3, 8
say: Here's a new tilemap with no tileset image. Until now, every tile of a map like this was the same plain square, so a floor and a wall looked alike.
click: editor:Tilemap.PlaceholderColors:add
editorset: Tilemap.PlaceholderColors:color:1 = #3A3F4B
click: editor:Tilemap.PlaceholderColors:add
editorset: Tilemap.PlaceholderColors:color:2 = #343844
click: editor:Tilemap.PlaceholderColors:add
editorset: Tilemap.PlaceholderColors:color:3 = #FF00FF
click: editor:Tilemap.PlaceholderColors:add
editorset: Tilemap.PlaceholderColors:color:4 = #99009A
explain: field:Tilemap.PlaceholderColors | Placeholder Colors | Its new Placeholder Colors give each tile number a color: tile 0 is the first, tile 1 the second, and so on. Two grays for the floor, and two pinks for walls.
explain: tiles:0 | The palette | The tile palette shows a tile for each color, so painting works without any art.
set: Tilemap.Tiles = 0101010101\n1010101010\n0101010101\n1010101010\n0101010101\n1010101010
play
expectdrawn: 1.5, -3.5 = #3A3F4B
expectdrawn: 0.5, -3.5 = #343844
stop
say: Filled with tiles 0 and 1 in turn, the floor is a checker, and every cell is easy to count.

chapter: Walls on a layer | Tops and faces
click: tiles:layer:+
expectselected: Tilemap Layer 2
set: Tilemap.SortByY = true
explain: field:Tilemap.SortByY | A wall layer | Walls go on a layer of their own that sorts by Y. A layer uses its map's colors, so tile 2 is the same pink here.
click: tiles:Rectangle
click: tiles:2
scenedrag: 0.5, -0.5 > 9.5, -0.5
click: tiles:3
scenedrag: 0.5, -1.5 > 9.5, -1.5
expecttile: Tilemap Layer 2 4, 0 = 2
expecttile: Tilemap Layer 2 4, 1 = 3
play
expectdrawn: 4.5, -0.5 = #FF00FF
expectdrawn: 4.5, -1.5 = #99009A
stop
say: The wall's top is one color and its front face another, all from tile numbers. When the art arrives, give the map its Image and the same numbers pick tiles from it.

chapter: A grid | Placeholder Grid
select: Tilemap
set: Tilemap.PlaceholderGrid = true
explain: field:Tilemap.PlaceholderGrid | Placeholder Grid | Placeholder Grid draws a thin line round each tile, a shade darker than it, so the cells show even on a floor of one color.
say: Agents set the colors the same way, as a list of hex colors on the tilemap.
